      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JAN HEWETT (1) boasts a strong record this journey here with four wins and three minors from 11 tries. Was out of the placings last time (23.16) at this track in a Grade 5, finishing sixth and beaten 12 lengths. Rates on top and should go close. ZIPPING BOTHAM (2) got the job done again after leading them home to make it two in a row, scoring at Murray Bridge Straight over 350m (19.61). One of main contenders. PAW PETROV (4) jumped from the inside and boxed on well to finish second last time, beaten 0.8 lengths (30.79) behind Hijinkery at Angle Park. Didn't win last time but still ran one of the quickest times on the card. Will give a great sight again. DURAN PANTERA (7) ran good time (38.02) when third last start over 643m at this track, the second placing in a row.",
